dho:p-dhp279-1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-dhp279 ;
    dho:segment "dhp279:1" ;
    dho:textEn "All things are not-self—"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sabbe dhammā anattā”ti,"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/dhp279/en/sujato#dhp279:1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn10-36.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn10 ;
    dho:segment "mn10:36.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of principles with respect to the five hindrances."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu dhammesu dhammānupassī viharati pañcasu nīvaraṇesu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn10/en/sujato#mn10:36.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn148-5.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn148 ;
    dho:segment "mn148:5.3" ;
    dho:textEn "There are the sense fields of sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, and ideas."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Rūpāyatanaṁ, saddāyatanaṁ, gandhāyatanaṁ, rasāyatanaṁ, phoṭṭhabbāyatanaṁ, dhammāyatanaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn148/en/sujato#mn148:5.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn148-6.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn148 ;
    dho:segment "mn148:6.8" ;
    dho:textEn "Mind consciousness arises dependent on the mind and ideas."@en ;
    dho:textPi "manañca paṭicca dhamme ca uppajjati manoviññāṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn148/en/sujato#mn148:6.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn43-19.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn43 ;
    dho:segment "mn43:19.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“The first absorption has five factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Paṭhamaṁ kho, āvuso, jhānaṁ pañcaṅgikaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato#mn43:19.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn43-19.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn43 ;
    dho:segment "mn43:19.3" ;
    dho:textEn "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idhāvuso, paṭhamaṁ jhānaṁ samāpannassa bhikkhuno vitakko ca vattati, vicāro ca pīti ca sukhañca cittekaggatā ca."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato#mn43:19.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn43-20.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn43 ;
    dho:segment "mn43:20.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“The first absorption has given up five factors and possesses five factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Paṭhamaṁ kho, āvuso, jhānaṁ pañcaṅgavippahīnaṁ, pañcaṅgasamannāgataṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato#mn43:20.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn43-20.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn43 ;
    dho:segment "mn43:20.3" ;
    dho:textEn "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt are given up."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idhāvuso, paṭhamaṁ jhānaṁ samāpannassa bhikkhuno kāmacchando pahīno hoti, byāpādo pahīno hoti, thinamiddhaṁ pahīnaṁ hoti, uddhaccakukkuccaṁ pahīnaṁ hoti, vicikicchā pahīnā hoti;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato#mn43:20.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn43-20.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn43 ;
    dho:segment "mn43:20.4" ;
    dho:textEn "Placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en ;
    dho:textPi "vitakko ca vattati, vicāro ca pīti ca sukhañca cittekaggatā ca."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato#mn43:20.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-mn44-12.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn44 ;
    dho:segment "mn44:12.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Unification of the mind is immersion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Yā kho, āvuso visākha, cittassa ekaggatā ayaṁ samādhi;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn44/en/sujato#mn44:12.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn11.3-10.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn11.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn11.3:10.2" ;
    dho:textEn "‘The teaching is well explained by the Buddha—apparent in the present life, immediately effective, inviting inspection, relevant, so that sensible people can know it for themselves.’"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“svākkhāto bhagavatā dhammo sandiṭṭhiko akāliko ehipassiko opaneyyiko paccattaṁ veditabbo viññūhī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn11.3/en/sujato#sn11.3:10.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.1-1.12 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.1:1.12" ;
    dho:textEn "They develop the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato#sn46.1:1.12"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.1-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.1:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, dragons grow and wax strong supported by the Himalayas, the king of mountains."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, himavantaṁ pabbatarājānaṁ nissāya nāgā kāyaṁ vaḍḍhenti, balaṁ gāhenti;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato#sn46.1:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.1-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.1:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "When they’re strong they dive into the pools. Then they dive into the lakes, the streams, the rivers, and finally the ocean. There they acquire a great and abundant body."@en ;
    dho:textPi "te tattha kāyaṁ vaḍḍhetvā balaṁ gāhetvā kusobbhe otaranti, kusobbhe otaritvā mahāsobbhe otaranti, mahāsobbhe otaritvā kunnadiyo otaranti, kunnadiyo otaritvā mahānadiyo otaranti, mahānadiyo otaritvā mahāsamuddasāgaraṁ otaranti; te tattha mahantattaṁ vepullattaṁ āpajjanti kāyena;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato#sn46.1:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.1-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.1:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu sīlaṁ nissāya sīle patiṭṭhāya satta bojjhaṅge bhāvento satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaronto mahantattaṁ vepullattaṁ pāpuṇāti dhammesu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato#sn46.1:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.1-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.1:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato#sn46.1:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.11-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.11 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.11:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, whatever living creatures engage in the four postures—"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ye keci pāṇā cattāro iriyāpathe kappenti—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.11/en/sujato#sn46.11:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.11-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.11 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.11:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "sometimes walking, sometimes standing, sometimes sitting, sometimes lying down—all do so depending on the earth and grounded on the earth."@en ;
    dho:textPi "kālena gamanaṁ, kālena ṭhānaṁ, kālena nisajjaṁ, kālena seyyaṁ, sabbe te pathaviṁ nissāya pathaviyaṁ patiṭṭhāya evamete cattāro iriyāpathe kappenti;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.11/en/sujato#sn46.11:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.11-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.11 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.11:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu sīlaṁ nissāya sīle patiṭṭhāya satta bojjhaṅge bhāveti, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaroti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.11/en/sujato#sn46.11:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.11-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.11 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.11:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.11/en/sujato#sn46.11:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.12-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.12 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.12:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sūriyassa, bhikkhave, udayato etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—aruṇuggaṁ;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.12/en/sujato#sn46.12:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.12-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.12 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.12:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ nimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—kalyāṇamittatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.12/en/sujato#sn46.12:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.12-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.12 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.12:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant with good friends can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.12/en/sujato#sn46.12:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.12-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.12 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.12:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.12/en/sujato#sn46.12:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.13-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.13 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.13:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sūriyassa, bhikkhave, udayato etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—aruṇuggaṁ;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.13/en/sujato#sn46.13:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.13-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.13 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.13:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—yonisomanasikāro."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.13/en/sujato#sn46.13:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.13-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.13 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.13:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant accomplished in rational application of mind can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.13/en/sujato#sn46.13:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.13-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.13 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.13:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.13/en/sujato#sn46.13:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.10 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.10" ;
    dho:textEn "“… which have freedom from death as their objective, destination, and culmination …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "amatogadhaṁ amataparāyanaṁ amatapariyosānaṁ …"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.10"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.11 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.11" ;
    dho:textEn "“… which slant, slope, and incline to extinguishment …"@en ;
    dho:textPi "nibbānaninnaṁ nibbānapoṇaṁ nibbānapabbhāraṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.11"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.12 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.12" ;
    dho:textEn "The seven awakening factors should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Imesaṁ kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu pañcannaṁ uddhambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ abhiññāya pariññāya parikkhayāya pahānāya ime satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvetabbā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.12"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, there are five higher fetters."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcimāni, bhikkhave, uddhambhāgiyāni saṁyojanāni."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "Desire for rebirth in the realm of luminous form, desire for rebirth in the formless realm, conceit, restlessness, and ignorance."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Rūparāgo, arūparāgo, māno, uddhaccaṁ, avijjā—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "The seven awakening factors should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Imesaṁ kho, bhikkhave, pañcannaṁ uddhambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ abhiññāya pariññāya parikkhayāya pahānāya satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvetabbā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.9" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which culminate in the removal of greed, hate, and delusion. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti rāgavinayapariyosānaṁ dosavinayapariyosānaṁ mohavinayapariyosānaṁ …"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.14-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.14 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.14:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Kassapa, I’ve rightly explained these seven awakening factors. When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, kassapa, bojjhaṅgā mayā sammadakkhātā bhāvitā bahulīkatā abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.14/en/sujato#sn46.14:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.14-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.14 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.14:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo kho, kassapa, mayā sammadakkhāto bhāvito bahulīkato abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo kho, kassapa, mayā sammadakkhāto bhāvito bahulīkato abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.14/en/sujato#sn46.14:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.14-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.14 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.14:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These are the seven awakening factors that I’ve rightly explained. When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, kassapa, satta bojjhaṅgā mayā sammadakkhātā bhāvitā bahulīkatā abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.14/en/sujato#sn46.14:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.15-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.15 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.15:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Moggallāna, I’ve rightly explained these seven awakening factors. When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, moggallāna, bojjhaṅgā mayā sammadakkhātā bhāvitā bahulīkatā abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.15/en/sujato#sn46.15:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.15-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.15 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.15:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo kho, moggallāna, mayā sammadakkhāto bhāvito bahulīkato abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo kho, moggallāna, mayā sammadakkhāto bhāvito bahulīkato abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.15/en/sujato#sn46.15:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.15-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.15 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.15:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These are the seven awakening factors that I’ve rightly explained. When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, moggallāna, satta bojjhaṅgā mayā sammadakkhātā bhāvitā bahulīkatā abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.15/en/sujato#sn46.15:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.16-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.16 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.16:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Sir, the Buddha has rightly explained these seven awakening factors. When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhante, bojjhaṅgā bhagavatā sammadakkhātā bhāvitā bahulīkatā abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.16/en/sujato#sn46.16:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.16-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.16 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.16:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo kho, bhante, bhagavatā sammadakkhāto bhāvito bahulīkato abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo kho, bhante, bhagavatā sammadakkhāto bhāvito bahulīkato abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.16/en/sujato#sn46.16:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.16-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.16 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.16:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These are the seven awakening factors that the Buddha has rightly explained. When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhante, satta bojjhaṅgā bhagavatā sammadakkhātā bhāvitā bahulīkatā abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.16/en/sujato#sn46.16:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.16-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.16 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.16:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "“Indeed, Cunda, these are awakening factors!"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Taggha, cunda, bojjhaṅgā;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.16/en/sujato#sn46.16:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.16-3.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.16 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.16:3.2" ;
    dho:textEn "and the Teacher concurred."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Samanuñño satthā ahosi."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.16/en/sujato#sn46.16:3.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.17-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.17 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.17:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to going from the near shore to the far shore."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā apārā pāraṁ gamanāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.17/en/sujato#sn46.17:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.17-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.17 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.17:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.17/en/sujato#sn46.17:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.17-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.17 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.17:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead to going from the near shore to the far shore."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā apārā pāraṁ gamanāya saṁvattantīti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.17/en/sujato#sn46.17:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.19-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.19 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.19:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they are noble and emancipating, and bring one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā ariyā niyyānikā nīyanti takkarassa sammā dukkhakkhayāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.19/en/sujato#sn46.19:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.19-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.19 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.19:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.19/en/sujato#sn46.19:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.19-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.19 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.19:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they are noble and emancipating, and bring one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā ariyā niyyānikā nīyanti takkarassa sammā dukkhakkhayāyā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.19/en/sujato#sn46.19:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, this body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ayaṁ kāyo āhāraṭṭhitiko, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhati, anāhāro no tiṭṭhati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, the five hindrances are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, pañca nīvaraṇā āhāraṭṭhitikā, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhanti, anāhārā no tiṭṭhanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-10.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:10.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā, sāvajjānavajjā dhammā, hīnapaṇītā dhammā, kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:10.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-10.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:10.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:10.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-10.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:10.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of investigation of principles, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:10.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-11.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:11.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are the elements of initiative, persistence, and exertion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, ārambhadhātu nikkamadhātu parakkamadhātu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:11.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-11.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:11.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:11.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-11.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:11.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of energy, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:11.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-12.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:12.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, pītisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:12.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-12.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:12.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:12.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-12.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:12.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of rapture, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:12.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-13.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:13.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is tranquility of the body and of the mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kāyapassaddhi, cittapassaddhi."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:13.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-13.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:13.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:13.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-13.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:13.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of tranquility, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:13.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-14.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:14.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are the basis of serenity and freedom from distraction."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, samathanimittaṁ abyagganimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:14.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-14.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:14.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:14.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-14.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:14.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of immersion, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:14.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-15.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:15.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:15.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-15.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:15.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:15.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-15.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:15.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of equanimity, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:15.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-16.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:16.1" ;
    dho:textEn "This body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ayaṁ kāyo āhāraṭṭhitiko, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhati, anāhāro no tiṭṭhati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:16.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-16.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:16.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, ime satta bojjhaṅgā āhāraṭṭhitikā, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhanti, anāhārā no tiṭṭhantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:16.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the feature of beauty."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, subhanimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā kāmacchandassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā kāmacchandassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-3.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:3.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the feature of aversion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, paṭighanimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:3.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā byāpādassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā byāpādassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-4.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:4.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is discontent, sloth, yawning, sleepiness after eating, and mental sluggishness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, arati tandi vijambhitā bhattasammado cetaso ca līnattaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:4.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-4.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:4.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:4.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-4.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:4.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā thinamiddhassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā thinamiddhassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:4.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-5.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:5.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the unsettled mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, cetaso avūpasamo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:5.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-5.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:5.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:5.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-5.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:5.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of restlessness and remorse, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:5.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-6.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:6.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, vicikicchāṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:6.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-6.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:6.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:6.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-6.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:6.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of doubt, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannāya vā vicikicchāya uppādāya, uppannāya vā vicikicchāya bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:6.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-7.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:7.1" ;
    dho:textEn "This body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ayaṁ kāyo āhāraṭṭhitiko, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhati, anāhāro no tiṭṭhati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:7.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-7.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:7.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, the five hindrances are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, ime pañca nīvaraṇā āhāraṭṭhitikā, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhanti, anāhārā no tiṭṭhanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:7.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-8.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:8.1" ;
    dho:textEn "This body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ayaṁ kāyo āhāraṭṭhitiko, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhati, anāhāro no tiṭṭhati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:8.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-8.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:8.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā āhāraṭṭhitikā, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhanti, anāhārā no tiṭṭhanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:8.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-9.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:9.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, satisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:9.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-9.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:9.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:9.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.2-9.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.2 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.2:9.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of mindfulness, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.2/en/sujato#sn46.2:9.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.20-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.20:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, the seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening, and extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā ekantanibbidāya virāgāya nirodhāya upasamāya abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato#sn46.20:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.20-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.20:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato#sn46.20:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.20-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.20:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening, and extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā ekantanibbidāya virāgāya nirodhāya upasamāya abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato#sn46.20:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.21-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.21 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.21:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicant, they’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“‘Bodhāya saṁvattantī’ti kho, bhikkhu, tasmā bojjhaṅgāti vuccanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.21/en/sujato#sn46.21:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.21-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.21 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.21:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhu, satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.21/en/sujato#sn46.21:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.21-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.21 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.21:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.21/en/sujato#sn46.21:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.21-2.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.21 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.21:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "They’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Bodhāya saṁvattantī’ti kho, bhikkhu, tasmā ‘bojjhaṅgā’ti vuccantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.21/en/sujato#sn46.21:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.22-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.22 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.22:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, I will teach you the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Satta vo, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅge desessāmi;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.22/en/sujato#sn46.22:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.22-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.22 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.22:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "And what are the seven awakening factors?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katame ca, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.22/en/sujato#sn46.22:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.22-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.22 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.22:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.22/en/sujato#sn46.22:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when you apply the mind irrationally, sensual desire,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ayoniso, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva kāmacchando uppajjati, uppanno ca kāmacchando bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "ill will,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppanno ceva byāpādo uppajjati, uppanno ca byāpādo bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "dullness and drowsiness,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppannañceva thinamiddhaṁ uppajjati, uppannañca thinamiddhaṁ bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "restlessness and remorse,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppannañceva uddhaccakukkuccaṁ uppajjati, uppannañca uddhaccakukkuccaṁ bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "and doubt arise, and once arisen they increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppannā ceva vicikicchā uppajjati, uppannā ca vicikicchā bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "And the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity don’t arise, or if they’ve already arisen, they cease."@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppanno ceva satisambojjhaṅgo nuppajjati, uppanno ca satisambojjhaṅgo nirujjhati …pe… anuppanno ceva upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo nuppajjati, uppanno ca upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo nirujjhati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When you apply the mind rationally, sensual desire,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yoniso ca kho, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva kāmacchando nuppajjati, uppanno ca kāmacchando pahīyati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "and doubt don’t arise, or if they’ve already arisen they’re given up."@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppannā ceva vicikicchā nuppajjati, uppannā ca vicikicchā pahīyati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity arise, and once they’ve arisen, they’re fully developed.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Anuppanno ceva satisambojjhaṅgo uppajjati, uppanno ca satisambojjhaṅgo bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati …pe… anuppanno ceva upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo uppajjati, uppanno ca upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.25-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.25 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.25:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.25/en/sujato#sn46.25:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.26-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.26 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.26:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, you should develop the path and the practice that leads to the ending of craving."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Yo, bhikkhave, maggo yā paṭipadā taṇhakkhayāya saṁvattati, taṁ maggaṁ taṁ paṭipadaṁ bhāvetha."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.26/en/sujato#sn46.26:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.26-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.26 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.26:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "It is the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.26/en/sujato#sn46.26:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.26-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.26 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.26:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.26/en/sujato#sn46.26:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.26-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.26 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.26:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Udāyī, it’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Idha, udāyi, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.26/en/sujato#sn46.26:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.26-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.26 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.26:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant develops the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.26/en/sujato#sn46.26:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.27-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.27 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.27:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, you should develop the path and the practice that leads to the cessation of craving."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Yo, bhikkhave, maggo yā paṭipadā taṇhānirodhāya saṁvattati, taṁ maggaṁ taṁ paṭipadaṁ bhāvetha."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.27/en/sujato#sn46.27:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.27-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.27 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.27:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "It is the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.27/en/sujato#sn46.27:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.27-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.27 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.27:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.27/en/sujato#sn46.27:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.27-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.27 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.27:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.27/en/sujato#sn46.27:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.27-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.27 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.27:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "This is how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to the cessation of craving.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā evaṁ bahulīkatā taṇhānirodhāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.27/en/sujato#sn46.27:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, I will teach you a path that helps penetration."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Nibbedhabhāgiyaṁ vo, bhikkhave, maggaṁ desessāmi;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "It is the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-1.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:1.9" ;
    dho:textEn "“Sir, how are the seven awakening factors developed and cultivated so as to lead to penetration?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“kathaṁ bhāvitā nu kho, bhante, satta bojjhaṅgā kathaṁ bahulīkatā nibbedhāya saṁvattantī”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:1.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Udāyī, it’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Idha, udāyi, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant develops the awakening factor of equanimity, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go. And it is abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ vipulaṁ mahaggataṁ appamāṇaṁ abyāpajjaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.28-2.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.28 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.28:2.9" ;
    dho:textEn "This is how are the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to penetration.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, udāyi, satta bojjhaṅgā evaṁ bahulīkatā nibbedhāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato#sn46.28:2.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.29-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.29 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.29:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, I do not see a single thing that, when it is developed and cultivated like this, leads to giving up the things that tighten the fetters like the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Nāhaṁ, bhikkhave, aññaṁ ekadhammampi samanupassāmi, yo evaṁ bhāvito bahulīkato saṁyojanīyānaṁ dhammānaṁ pahānāya saṁvattati, yathayidaṁ, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.29/en/sujato#sn46.29:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.29-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.29 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.29:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.29/en/sujato#sn46.29:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.29-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.29 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.29:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.29/en/sujato#sn46.29:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.29-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.29 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.29:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to lead to giving up the things that tighten the fetters."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā evaṁ bahulīkatā saṁyojanīyānaṁ dhammānaṁ pahānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.29/en/sujato#sn46.29:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-1.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:1.9" ;
    dho:textEn "as they recollect and think about that teaching."@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tathā vūpakaṭṭho viharanto taṁ dhammaṁ anussarati anuvitakketi."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:1.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of mindfulness;"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhu tathā vūpakaṭṭho viharanto taṁ dhammaṁ anussarati anuvitakketi, satisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "As they live mindfully in this way they investigate, explore, and inquire into that teaching with wisdom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tathā sato viharanto taṁ dhammaṁ paññāya pavicinati pavicarati parivīmaṁsamāpajjati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of investigation of principles;"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhu tathā sato viharanto taṁ dhammaṁ paññāya pavicinati pavicarati parivīmaṁsamāpajjati, dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "As they investigate principles with wisdom in this way their energy is roused up and unflagging."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tassa taṁ dhammaṁ paññāya pavicinato pavicarato parivīmaṁsamāpajjato āraddhaṁ hoti vīriyaṁ asallīnaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-4.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:4.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of energy; they develop it and perfect it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno taṁ dhammaṁ paññāya pavicinato pavicarato parivīmaṁsamāpajjato āraddhaṁ hoti vīriyaṁ asallīnaṁ, vīriyasambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti; vīriyasambojjhaṅgaṁ tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhu bhāveti; vīriyasambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:4.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-4.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:4.2" ;
    dho:textEn "When they’re energetic, rapture not of the flesh arises."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Āraddhavīriyassa uppajjati pīti nirāmisā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:4.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-5.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:5.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of rapture; they develop it and perfect it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno āraddhavīriyassa uppajjati pīti nirāmisā, pītisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti; pītisambojjhaṅgaṁ tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhu bhāveti; pītisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:5.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-5.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:5.2" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is full of rapture, the body and mind become tranquil."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Pītimanassa kāyopi passambhati, cittampi passambhati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:5.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-6.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:6.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of tranquility; they develop it and perfect it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pītimanassa kāyopi passambhati cittampi passambhati, passaddhisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti; passaddhisambojjhaṅgaṁ tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhu bhāveti; passaddhisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:6.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-6.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:6.2" ;
    dho:textEn "When the body is tranquil and one feels bliss, the mind becomes immersed in samādhi."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Passaddhakāyassa sukhino cittaṁ samādhiyati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:6.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-7.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:7.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of immersion; they develop it and perfect it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno passaddhakāyassa sukhino cittaṁ samādhiyati, samādhisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti; samādhisambojjhaṅgaṁ tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhu bhāveti; samādhisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:7.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-7.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:7.2" ;
    dho:textEn "They closely watch over that mind immersed in samādhi."@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tathāsamāhitaṁ cittaṁ sādhukaṁ ajjhupekkhitā hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:7.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-8.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:8.1" ;
    dho:textEn "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of equanimity; they develop it and perfect it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ samaye, bhikkhave, bhikkhu tathāsamāhitaṁ cittaṁ sādhukaṁ ajjhupekkhitā hoti, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno āraddho hoti; upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhu bhāveti; upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhikkhuno bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:8.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way they can expect seven fruits and benefits."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitesu kho, bhikkhave, sattasu sambojjhaṅgesu evaṁ bahulīkatesu satta phalā sattānisaṁsā pāṭikaṅkhā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.10 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.10" ;
    dho:textEn "When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way these are the seven fruits and benefits they can expect.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitesu kho, bhikkhave, sattasu bojjhaṅgesu evaṁ bahulīkatesu ime satta phalā sattānisaṁsā pāṭikaṅkhā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.10"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.2" ;
    dho:textEn "What seven?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katame satta phalā sattānisaṁsā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.3" ;
    dho:textEn "They attain enlightenment early on in this very life."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.4" ;
    dho:textEn "If not, they attain enlightenment at the time of death."@en ;
    dho:textPi "No ce diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti, atha maraṇakāle aññaṁ ārādheti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.5" ;
    dho:textEn "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters, they’re extinguished between one life and the next."@en ;
    dho:textPi "No ce diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce maraṇakāle aññaṁ ārādheti, atha pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā antarāparinibbāyī hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.6" ;
    dho:textEn "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished upon landing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "No ce diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce maraṇakāle aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā antarāparinibbāyī hoti, atha pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā upahaccaparinibbāyī hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.7" ;
    dho:textEn "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished without extra effort."@en ;
    dho:textPi "No ce diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce maraṇakāle aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā antarāparinibbāyī hoti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā upahaccaparinibbāyī hoti, atha pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā asaṅkhāraparinibbāyī hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.8" ;
    dho:textEn "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished with extra effort."@en ;
    dho:textPi "No ce diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce maraṇakāle aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā antarāparinibbāyī hoti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā upahaccaparinibbāyī hoti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā asaṅkhāraparinibbāyī hoti, atha pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā sasaṅkhāraparinibbāyī hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.9" ;
    dho:textEn "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they head upstream, going to the Akaniṭṭha realm."@en ;
    dho:textPi "No ce diṭṭheva dhamme paṭikacca aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce maraṇakāle aññaṁ ārādheti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā antarāparinibbāyī hoti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā upahaccaparinibbāyī hoti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā asaṅkhāraparinibbāyī hoti, no ce pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā sasaṅkhāraparinibbāyī hoti, atha pañcannaṁ orambhāgiyānaṁ saṁyojanānaṁ parikkhayā uddhaṁsoto hoti akaniṭṭhagāmī."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.31-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.31 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.31:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, whatever qualities are skillful, part of the skillful, on the side of the skillful, all of them are rooted in diligence and meet at diligence, and diligence is said to be the best of them."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ye keci, bhikkhave, dhammā kusalā kusalabhāgiyā kusalapakkhikā, sabbe te appamādamūlakā appamādasamosaraṇā; appamādo tesaṁ dhammānaṁ aggamakkhāyati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.31/en/sujato#sn46.31:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.31-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.31 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.31:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant who is diligent can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Appamattassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.31/en/sujato#sn46.31:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.31-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.31 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.31:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.31/en/sujato#sn46.31:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.32-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.32 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.32:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, whatever qualities are skillful, part of the skillful, on the side of the skillful, all of them are rooted in rational application of mind and meet at rational application of mind, and rational application of mind is said to be the best of them."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ye keci, bhikkhave, dhammā kusalā kusalabhāgiyā kusalapakkhikā, sabbe te yonisomanasikāramūlakā yonisomanasikārasamosaraṇā; yonisomanasikāro tesaṁ dhammānaṁ aggamakkhāyati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.32/en/sujato#sn46.32:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.32-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.32 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.32:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant accomplished in rational application of mind can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.32/en/sujato#sn46.32:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.32-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.32 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.32:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.32/en/sujato#sn46.32:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, there are these five corruptions of native gold. When native gold is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant, but is brittle and not completely ready for working."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcime, bhikkhave, jātarūpassa upakkilesā, yehi upakkilesehi upakkiliṭṭhaṁ jātarūpaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā upeti kammāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Iron,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ayo, bhikkhave, jātarūpassa upakkileso, yena upakkilesena upakkiliṭṭhaṁ jātarūpaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā upeti kammāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "copper,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Lohaṁ, bhikkhave, jātarūpassa upakkileso, yena upakkilesena upakkiliṭṭhaṁ jātarūpaṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "tin,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "tipu, bhikkhave, jātarūpassa upakkileso …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "lead,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "sīsaṁ, bhikkhave, jātarūpassa upakkileso …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "and silver."@en ;
    dho:textPi "sajjhu, bhikkhave, jātarūpassa upakkileso, yena upakkilesena upakkiliṭṭhaṁ jātarūpaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā upeti kammāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-1.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "When native gold is corrupted by these five corruptions it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant, but is brittle and not completely ready for working."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, pañca jātarūpassa upakkilesā, yehi upakkilesehi upakkiliṭṭhaṁ jātarūpaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā upeti kammāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, bhikkhave, pañcime cittassa upakkilesā, yehi upakkilesehi upakkiliṭṭhaṁ cittaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā samādhiyati āsavānaṁ khayāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kāmacchando, bhikkhave, cittassa upakkileso, yena upakkilesena upakkiliṭṭhaṁ cittaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā samādhiyati āsavānaṁ khayāya …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These are the five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "ime kho, bhikkhave, pañca cittassa upakkilesā, yehi upakkilesehi upakkiliṭṭhaṁ cittaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā samādhiyati āsavānaṁ khayāyā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.34-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.34 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.34:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, these seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anupakkilesā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.34/en/sujato#sn46.34:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.34-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.34 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.34:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.34/en/sujato#sn46.34:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.34-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.34 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.34:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anupakkilesā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.34/en/sujato#sn46.34:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.35-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.35 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.35:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when you apply the mind irrationally, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt arise, and once arisen they increase and grow.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ayoniso, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva kāmacchando uppajjati, uppanno ca kāmacchando bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppanno ceva byāpādo uppajjati, uppanno ca byāpādo bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppannañceva thinamiddhaṁ uppajjati, uppannañca thinamiddhaṁ bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppannañceva uddhaccakukkuccaṁ uppajjati, uppannañca uddhaccakukkuccaṁ bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppannā ceva vicikicchā uppajjati, uppannā ca vicikicchā bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.35/en/sujato#sn46.35:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.35-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.35 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.35:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when you apply the mind rationally, the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity arise, and once they’ve arisen, they’re fully developed.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Yoniso ca kho, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva satisambojjhaṅgo uppajjati, uppanno ca satisambojjhaṅgo bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati …pe… anuppanno ceva upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo uppajjati, uppanno ca upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.35/en/sujato#sn46.35:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.36-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.36 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.36:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to growth and progress."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā buddhiyā aparihānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.36/en/sujato#sn46.36:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.36-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.36 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.36:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.36/en/sujato#sn46.36:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.36-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.36 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.36:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to growth and progress.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā buddhiyā aparihānāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.36/en/sujato#sn46.36:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, there are these five obstacles and hindrances, corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcime, bhikkhave, āvaraṇā nīvaraṇā cetaso upakkilesā paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Sensual desire,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kāmacchando, bhikkhave, āvaraṇo nīvaraṇo cetaso upakkileso paññāya dubbalīkaraṇo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "ill will,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Byāpādo, bhikkhave, āvaraṇo nīvaraṇo cetaso upakkileso paññāya dubbalīkaraṇo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "dullness and drowsiness,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Thinamiddhaṁ, bhikkhave, āvaraṇaṁ nīvaraṇaṁ cetaso upakkilesaṁ paññāya dubbalīkaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "restlessness and remorse,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Uddhaccakukkuccaṁ, bhikkhave, āvaraṇaṁ nīvaraṇaṁ cetaso upakkilesaṁ paññāya dubbalīkaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "and doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Vicikicchā, bhikkhave, āvaraṇā nīvaraṇā cetaso upakkilesā paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "These are the five obstacles and hindrances, corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, pañca āvaraṇā nīvaraṇā cetaso upakkilesā paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "There are these seven awakening factors that are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anupakkilesā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anupakkilesā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattantīti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, sometimes a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly, and actively listens to the teaching. At such a time the five hindrances are absent, and the seven awakening factors are fully developed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye ariyasāvako aṭṭhiṁ katvā manasi katvā sabbaṁ cetaso samannāharitvā ohitasoto dhammaṁ suṇāti, imassa pañca nīvaraṇā tasmiṁ samaye na honti. Satta bojjhaṅgā tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "What are the five hindrances that are absent?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katame pañca nīvaraṇā tasmiṁ samaye na honti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "Sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kāmacchandanīvaraṇaṁ tasmiṁ samaye na hoti, byāpādanīvaraṇaṁ tasmiṁ samaye na hoti, thinamiddhanīvaraṇaṁ tasmiṁ samaye na hoti, uddhaccakukkuccanīvaraṇaṁ tasmiṁ samaye na hoti, vicikicchānīvaraṇaṁ tasmiṁ samaye na hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what are the seven awakening factors that are fully developed?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katame satta bojjhaṅgā tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchanti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-3.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:3.2" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:3.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "Sometimes a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly, and actively listens to the teaching. At such a time the five hindrances are absent, and the seven awakening factors are fully developed.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye ariyasāvako aṭṭhiṁ katvā manasi katvā sabbaṁ cetaso samannāharitvā ohitasoto dhammaṁ suṇāti, imassa pañca nīvaraṇā tasmiṁ samaye na honti. Ime satta bojjhaṅgā tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.4-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.4 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.4:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“There are these seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, āvuso, bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.4/en/sujato#sn46.4:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.4-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.4 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.4:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo, dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgo, vīriyasambojjhaṅgo, pītisambojjhaṅgo, passaddhisambojjhaṅgo, samādhisambojjhaṅgo, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.4/en/sujato#sn46.4:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.4-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.4 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.4:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These are the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ime kho, āvuso, satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.4/en/sujato#sn46.4:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, these five hindrances are destroyers of sight, vision, and knowledge. They block wisdom, they’re on the side of distress, and they don’t lead to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcime, bhikkhave, nīvaraṇā andhakaraṇā acakkhukaraṇā aññāṇakaraṇā paññānirodhikā vighātapakkhiyā anibbānasaṁvattanikā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kāmacchandanīvaraṇaṁ, bhikkhave, andhakaraṇaṁ acakkhukaraṇaṁ aññāṇakaraṇaṁ paññānirodhikaṁ vighātapakkhiyaṁ anibbānasaṁvattanikaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.4" ;
    dho:textPi "Byāpādanīvaraṇaṁ, bhikkhave …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.5" ;
    dho:textPi "thinamiddhanīvaraṇaṁ, bhikkhave …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.6" ;
    dho:textPi "uddhaccakukkuccanīvaraṇaṁ, bhikkhave …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.7" ;
    dho:textPi "vicikicchānīvaraṇaṁ, bhikkhave, andhakaraṇaṁ acakkhukaraṇaṁ aññāṇakaraṇaṁ paññānirodhikaṁ vighātapakkhiyaṁ anibbānasaṁvattanikaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "These five hindrances are destroyers of sight, vision, and knowledge. They block wisdom, they’re on the side of distress, and they don’t lead to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, pañca nīvaraṇā andhakaraṇā acakkhukaraṇā aññāṇakaraṇā paññānirodhikā vighātapakkhiyā anibbānasaṁvattanikā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā cakkhukaraṇā ñāṇakaraṇā paññābuddhiyā avighātapakkhiyā nibbānasaṁvattanikā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, cakkhukaraṇo ñāṇakaraṇo paññābuddhiyo avighātapakkhiyo nibbānasaṁvattaniko …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, cakkhukaraṇo ñāṇakaraṇo paññābuddhiyo avighātapakkhiyo nibbānasaṁvattaniko."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā cakkhukaraṇā ñāṇakaraṇā paññābuddhiyā avighātapakkhiyā nibbānasaṁvattanikā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.41-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.41 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.41:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, all the ascetics and brahmins in the past who have given up the three discriminations have done so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ye hi keci, bhikkhave, atītamaddhānaṁ samaṇā vā brāhmaṇā vā tisso vidhā pajahiṁsu, sabbe te sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ bhāvitattā bahulīkatattā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.41/en/sujato#sn46.41:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.41-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.41 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.41:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "All the ascetics and brahmins in the future who will give up the three discriminations will do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ye hi keci, bhikkhave, anāgatamaddhānaṁ samaṇā vā brāhmaṇā vā tisso vidhā pajahissanti, sabbe te sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ bhāvitattā bahulīkatattā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.41/en/sujato#sn46.41:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.41-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.41 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.41:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "All the ascetics and brahmins in the present who are giving up the three discriminations do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ye hi keci, bhikkhave, etarahi samaṇā vā brāhmaṇā vā tisso vidhā pajahanti, sabbe te sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ bhāvitattā bahulīkatattā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.41/en/sujato#sn46.41:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.41-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.41 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.41:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgassa …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.41/en/sujato#sn46.41:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.41-1.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.41 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.41:1.9" ;
    dho:textEn "and present who give up the three discriminations do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "pajahanti, sabbe te imesaṁyeva sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ bhāvitattā bahulīkatattā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.41/en/sujato#sn46.41:1.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.43-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.43 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.43:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, I will teach you a path for crushing Māra’s army."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Mārasenappamaddanaṁ vo, bhikkhave, maggaṁ desessāmi;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.43/en/sujato#sn46.43:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.43-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.43 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.43:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "It is the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "satta bojjhaṅgā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.43/en/sujato#sn46.43:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.43-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.43 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.43:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.43/en/sujato#sn46.43:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.43-1.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.43 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.43:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "This is the path for crushing Māra’s army.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayaṁ kho, bhikkhave, mārasenappamaddano maggo”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.43/en/sujato#sn46.43:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.48-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.48 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.48:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ādiccassa, bhikkhave, udayato etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—aruṇuggaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.48/en/sujato#sn46.48:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.48-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.48 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.48:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—kalyāṇamittatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.48/en/sujato#sn46.48:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.48-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.48 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.48:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant with good friends can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.48/en/sujato#sn46.48:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.48-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.48 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.48:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.48/en/sujato#sn46.48:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.49-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.49 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.49:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Taking into account interior factors, mendicants, I do not see a single one that gives rise to the seven awakening factors like rational application of mind. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ajjhattikaṁ, bhikkhave, aṅganti karitvā nāññaṁ ekaṅgampi samanupassāmi sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya, yathayidaṁ—bhikkhave, yonisomanasikāro."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.49/en/sujato#sn46.49:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.49-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.49 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.49:1.2" ;
    dho:textPi "Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.49/en/sujato#sn46.49:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.49-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.49 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.49:1.4" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.49/en/sujato#sn46.49:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.49-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.49 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.49:1.5" ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.49/en/sujato#sn46.49:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.49-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.49 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.49:1.6" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu yonisomanasikārasampanno satta bojjhaṅge bhāveti, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarotī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.49/en/sujato#sn46.49:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.5-1.11 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.5 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.5:1.11" ;
    dho:textEn "They’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Bodhāya saṁvattantīti, bhikkhu, tasmā ‘bojjhaṅgā’ti vuccantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.5/en/sujato#sn46.5:1.11"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.5-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.5 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.5:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicant, they’re called awakening factors because they lead to awakening."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Bodhāya saṁvattantīti kho, bhikkhu, tasmā ‘bojjhaṅgā’ti vuccanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.5/en/sujato#sn46.5:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.5-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.5 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.5:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhu, satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.5/en/sujato#sn46.5:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.5-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.5 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.5:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.5/en/sujato#sn46.5:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.50-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.50 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.50:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Taking into account exterior factors, mendicants, I do not see a single one that gives rise to the seven awakening factors like good friendship. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Bāhiraṁ, bhikkhave, aṅganti karitvā nāññaṁ ekaṅgampi samanupassāmi sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya, yathayidaṁ—bhikkhave, kalyāṇamittatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.50/en/sujato#sn46.50:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.50-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.50 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.50:1.2" ;
    dho:textPi "Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.50/en/sujato#sn46.50:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.50-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.50 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.50:1.4" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.50/en/sujato#sn46.50:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.50-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.50 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.50:1.5" ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.50/en/sujato#sn46.50:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.50-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.50 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.50:1.6" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu kalyāṇamitto satta bojjhaṅge bhāveti, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarotī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.50/en/sujato#sn46.50:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, I will teach you what fuels and what starves the five hindrances and the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcannañca, bhikkhave, nīvaraṇānaṁ sattannañca bojjhaṅgānaṁ āhārañca anāhārañca desessāmi;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā kāmacchandassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā kāmacchandassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the feature of beauty."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, subhanimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā kāmacchandassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā kāmacchandassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-10.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:10.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of tranquility, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:10.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-10.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:10.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is tranquility of the body and of the mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kāyappassaddhi cittappassaddhi."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:10.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-10.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:10.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:10.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-10.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:10.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of tranquility, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:10.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-11.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:11.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of immersion, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:11.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-11.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:11.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are the basis of serenity and freedom from distraction."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, samathanimittaṁ abyagganimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:11.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-11.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:11.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:11.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-11.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:11.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of immersion, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:11.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-12.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:12.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of equanimity, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:12.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-12.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:12.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:12.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-12.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:12.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:12.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-12.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:12.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of equanimity, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:12.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-13.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:13.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the feature of ugliness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, asubhanimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:13.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-13.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:13.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:13.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-13.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:13.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, starves its increase and growth."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā kāmacchandassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā kāmacchandassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:13.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-14.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:14.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the heart’s release by love."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, mettācetovimutti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:14.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-14.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:14.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:14.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-14.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:14.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, starves its increase and growth."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā byāpādassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā byāpādassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:14.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-15.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:15.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are the elements of initiative, persistence, and exertion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, ārambhadhātu nikkamadhātu parakkamadhātu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:15.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-15.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:15.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:15.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-15.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:15.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, starves their increase and growth."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā thinamiddhassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā thinamiddhassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:15.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-16.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:16.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the settled mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, cetaso vūpasamo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:16.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-16.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:16.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:16.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-16.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:16.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of restlessness and remorse, or, when they have arisen, starves their increase and growth."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:16.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-17.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:17.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā sāvajjānavajjā dhammā hīnapaṇītā dhammā kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:17.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-17.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:17.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:17.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-17.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:17.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of doubt, or, when it has arisen, starves its increase and growth."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannāya vā vicikicchāya uppādāya, uppannāya vā vicikicchāya bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:17.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-18.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:18.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, satisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:18.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-18.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:18.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:18.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-18.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:18.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of mindfulness, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:18.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-19.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:19.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā sāvajjānavajjā dhammā hīnapaṇītā dhammā kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:19.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-19.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:19.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:19.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-19.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:19.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of investigation of principles, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:19.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā byāpādassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā byāpādassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the feature of aversion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, paṭighanimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā byāpādassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā byāpādassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-20.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:20.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are the elements of initiative, persistence, and exertion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, ārambhadhātu nikkamadhātu parakkamadhātu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:20.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-20.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:20.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:20.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-20.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:20.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of energy, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:20.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-21.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:21.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, pītisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:21.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-21.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:21.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:21.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-21.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:21.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of rapture, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:21.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-22.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:22.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is tranquility of the body and of the mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kāyappassaddhi cittappassaddhi."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:22.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-22.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:22.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:22.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-22.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:22.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of tranquility, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:22.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-23.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:23.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are the basis of serenity and freedom from distraction."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, samathanimittaṁ abyagganimittaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:23.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-23.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:23.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:23.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-23.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:23.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of immersion, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:23.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-24.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:24.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:24.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-24.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:24.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Not frequently applying the mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha amanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:24.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-24.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:24.4" ;
    dho:textEn "starves the arising of the awakening factor of equanimity, or, when it has arisen, starves its full development.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamanāhāro anuppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:24.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā thinamiddhassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā thinamiddhassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-3.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:3.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is discontent, sloth, yawning, sleepiness after eating, and mental sluggishness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, arati tandi vijambhitā bhattasammado cetaso ca līnattaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:3.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā thinamiddhassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā thinamiddhassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-4.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:4.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of restlessness and remorse, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:4.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-4.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:4.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There is the unsettled mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, cetaso avūpasamo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:4.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-4.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:4.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to that"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:4.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-4.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:4.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of restlessness and remorse, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā uddhaccakukkuccassa bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:4.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-5.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:5.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of doubt, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannāya vā vicikicchāya uppādāya, uppannāya vā vicikicchāya bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:5.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-5.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:5.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, vicikicchāṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:5.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-5.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:5.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent irrational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha ayonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:5.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-5.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:5.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of doubt, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannāya vā vicikicchāya uppādāya, uppannāya vā vicikicchāya bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:5.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-6.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:6.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of mindfulness, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:6.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-6.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:6.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, satisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:6.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-6.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:6.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:6.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-6.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:6.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of mindfulness, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā satisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:6.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-7.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:7.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of investigation of principles, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:7.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-7.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:7.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā sāvajjānavajjā dhammā hīnapaṇītā dhammā kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:7.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-7.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:7.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:7.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-7.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:7.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of investigation of principles, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:7.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-8.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:8.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of energy, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:8.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-8.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:8.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are the elements of initiative, persistence, and exertion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, ārambhadhātu nikkamadhātu parakkamadhātu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:8.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-8.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:8.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:8.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-8.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:8.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of energy, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:8.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-9.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:9.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of rapture, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ko ca, bhikkhave, āhāro anuppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:9.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-9.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:9.2" ;
    dho:textEn "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, pītisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:9.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-9.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:9.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Frequent rational application of mind to them"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Tattha yonisomanasikārabahulīkāro—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:9.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-9.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:9.4" ;
    dho:textEn "fuels the arising of the awakening factor of rapture, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayamāhāro anuppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa uppādāya, uppannassa vā pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya pāripūriyā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:9.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-10.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:10.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what is the way in which the seven awakening factors become fourteen?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katamo ca, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma satta bojjhaṅgā catuddasa honti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:10.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-10.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:10.2" ;
    dho:textEn "Mindfulness of internal things is the awakening factor of mindfulness; and mindfulness of external things is also the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, ajjhattaṁ dhammesu sati tadapi satisambojjhaṅgo, yadapi bahiddhā dhammesu sati tadapi satisambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:10.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-10.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:10.3" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of mindfulness’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Satisambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:10.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-11.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:11.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Investigating, exploring, and inquiring into internal things with wisdom is the awakening factor of investigation of principles; and investigating, exploring, and inquiring into external things with wisdom is also the awakening factor of investigation of principles."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, ajjhattaṁ dhammesu paññāya pavicinati pavicarati parivīmaṁsamāpajjati tadapi dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgo, yadapi bahiddhā dhammesu paññāya pavicinati pavicarati parivīmaṁsamāpajjati tadapi dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:11.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-11.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:11.2" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of investigation of principles’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:11.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-12.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:12.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Physical energy is the awakening factor of energy; and mental energy is also the awakening factor of energy."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, kāyikaṁ vīriyaṁ tadapi vīriyasambojjhaṅgo, yadapi cetasikaṁ vīriyaṁ tadapi vīriyasambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:12.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-12.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:12.2" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of energy’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Vīriyasambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:12.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-13.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:13.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Rapture while placing the mind and keeping it connected is the awakening factor of rapture; and rapture without placing the mind and keeping it connected is also the awakening factor of rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, savitakkasavicārā pīti tadapi pītisambojjhaṅgo, yadapi avitakkaavicārā pīti tadapi pītisambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:13.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-13.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:13.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of rapture’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Pītisambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:13.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-14.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:14.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Physical tranquility is the awakening factor of tranquility; and mental tranquility is also the awakening factor of tranquility."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, kāyappassaddhi tadapi passaddhisambojjhaṅgo, yadapi cittappassaddhi tadapi passaddhisambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:14.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-14.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:14.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of tranquility’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Passaddhisambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:14.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-15.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:15.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Immersion while placing the mind and keeping it connected is the awakening factor of immersion; and immersion without placing the mind and keeping it connected is also the awakening factor of immersion."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, savitakko savicāro samādhi tadapi samādhisambojjhaṅgo, yadapi avitakkaavicāro samādhi tadapi samādhisambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:15.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-15.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:15.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of immersion’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Samādhisambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:15.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-16.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:16.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Equanimity for internal things is the awakening factor of equanimity; and equanimity for external things is also the awakening factor of equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, ajjhattaṁ dhammesu upekkhā tadapi upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, yadapi bahiddhā dhammesu upekkhā tadapi upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:16.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-16.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:16.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of equanimity’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:16.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-16.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:16.3" ;
    dho:textEn "This is the way in which the seven awakening factors become fourteen.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ayaṁ kho, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma satta bojjhaṅgā catuddasā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:16.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what is the way in which the five hindrances become ten?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katamo ca, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma pañca nīvaraṇā dasa honti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.10 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.10" ;
    dho:textEn "Doubt about internal things is a hindrance; and doubt about external things is also a hindrance."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, ajjhattaṁ dhammesu vicikicchā tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ, yadapi bahiddhā dhammesu vicikicchā tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.10"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.11 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.11" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the hindrance of doubt’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Vicikicchānīvaraṇan’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.11"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.12 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.12" ;
    dho:textEn "This is the way in which the five hindrances become ten."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ayaṁ kho, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma pañca nīvaraṇā dasa honti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.12"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.2" ;
    dho:textEn "Sensual desire for what is internal is a hindrance; and sensual desire for what is external is also a hindrance."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, ajjhattaṁ kāmacchando tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ, yadapi bahiddhā kāmacchando tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.3" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the hindrance of sensual desire’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Kāmacchandanīvaraṇan’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.4" ;
    dho:textEn "Ill will for what is internal is a hindrance; and ill will for what is external is also a hindrance."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, ajjhattaṁ byāpādo tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ, yadapi bahiddhā byāpādo tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.5" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the hindrance of ill will’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Byāpādanīvaraṇan’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.6" ;
    dho:textEn "Dullness is a hindrance; and drowsiness is also a hindrance."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, thinaṁ tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ, yadapi middhaṁ tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.7" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the hindrance of dullness and drowsiness’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Thinamiddhanīvaraṇan’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.8" ;
    dho:textEn "Restlessness is a hindrance; and remorse is also a hindrance."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yadapi, bhikkhave, uddhaccaṁ tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ, yadapi kukkuccaṁ tadapi nīvaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.9" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how what is concisely referred to as ‘the hindrance of restlessness and remorse’ becomes twofold."@en ;
    dho:textPi "‘Uddhaccakukkuccanīvaraṇan’ti iti hidaṁ uddesaṁ gacchati. Tadamināpetaṁ pariyāyena dvayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-10.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:10.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye uddhataṁ cittaṁ hoti, akālo tasmiṁ samaye dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:10.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-10.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:10.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s hard to settle a restless mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Uddhataṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi duvūpasamayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:10.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-11.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:11.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Suppose someone wanted to extinguish a great mass of fire."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, puriso mahantaṁ aggikkhandhaṁ nibbāpetukāmo assa."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:11.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-11.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:11.2" ;
    dho:textEn "If they toss dry grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, blow on it, and don’t scatter dirt on it,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tattha sukkhāni ceva tiṇāni pakkhipeyya, sukkhāni ca gomayāni pakkhipeyya, sukkhāni ca kaṭṭhāni pakkhipeyya, mukhavātañca dadeyya, na ca paṁsukena okireyya;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:11.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-11.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:11.3" ;
    dho:textEn "could they extinguish it?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "bhabbo nu kho so puriso mahantaṁ aggikkhandhaṁ nibbāpetun”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:11.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-12.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:12.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“In the same way, when the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Evameva kho, bhikkhave, yasmiṁ samaye uddhataṁ cittaṁ hoti, akālo tasmiṁ samaye dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:12.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-13.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:13.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiñca kho, bhikkhave, samaye uddhataṁ cittaṁ hoti, kālo tasmiṁ samaye passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:13.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-13.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:13.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s easy to settle a restless mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Uddhataṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi suvūpasamayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:13.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-14.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:14.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Suppose someone wanted to extinguish a great mass of fire."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, puriso mahantaṁ aggikkhandhaṁ nibbāpetukāmo assa."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:14.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-14.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:14.2" ;
    dho:textEn "If they toss wet grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, spray it with water, and scatter dirt on it,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tattha allāni ceva tiṇāni pakkhipeyya, allāni ca gomayāni pakkhipeyya, allāni ca kaṭṭhāni pakkhipeyya, udakavātañca dadeyya, paṁsukena ca okireyya;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:14.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-14.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:14.3" ;
    dho:textEn "could they extinguish it?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "bhabbo nu kho so puriso mahantaṁ aggikkhandhaṁ nibbāpetun”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:14.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-15.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:15.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“In the same way, when the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Evameva kho, bhikkhave, yasmiṁ samaye uddhataṁ cittaṁ hoti, kālo tasmiṁ samaye passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:15.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-15.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:15.4" ;
    dho:textEn "But mindfulness is always useful, I say.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satiñca khvāhaṁ, bhikkhave, sabbatthikaṁ vadāmī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:15.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-4.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:4.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye līnaṁ cittaṁ hoti, akālo tasmiṁ samaye passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:4.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-4.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:4.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s hard to stimulate a sluggish mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Līnaṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi dussamuṭṭhāpayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:4.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-5.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:5.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Suppose someone wanted to make a small fire flare up."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, puriso parittaṁ aggiṁ ujjāletukāmo assa."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:5.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-5.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:5.2" ;
    dho:textEn "If they toss wet grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, spray it with water, and scatter dirt on it,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tattha allāni ceva tiṇāni pakkhipeyya, allāni ca gomayāni pakkhipeyya, allāni ca kaṭṭhāni pakkhipeyya, udakavātañca dadeyya, paṁsukena ca okireyya;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:5.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-5.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:5.3" ;
    dho:textEn "could they make it flare up?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "bhabbo nu kho so puriso parittaṁ aggiṁ ujjāletun”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:5.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-6.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:6.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“In the same way, when the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Evameva kho, bhikkhave, yasmiṁ samaye līnaṁ cittaṁ hoti, akālo tasmiṁ samaye passaddhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo samādhisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, akālo upekkhāsambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:6.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-7.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:7.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiñca kho, bhikkhave, samaye līnaṁ cittaṁ hoti, kālo tasmiṁ samaye dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:7.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-7.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:7.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Because it’s easy to stimulate a sluggish mind with these things."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Līnaṁ, bhikkhave, cittaṁ taṁ etehi dhammehi susamuṭṭhāpayaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:7.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-8.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:8.1" ;
    dho:textEn "Suppose someone wanted to make a small fire flare up."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, puriso parittaṁ aggiṁ ujjāletukāmo assa."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:8.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-8.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:8.2" ;
    dho:textEn "If they toss dry grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, blow on it, and don’t scatter dirt on it,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "So tattha sukkhāni ceva tiṇāni pakkhipeyya, sukkhāni gomayāni pakkhipeyya, sukkhāni kaṭṭhāni pakkhipeyya, mukhavātañca dadeyya, na ca paṁsukena okireyya;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:8.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-8.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:8.3" ;
    dho:textEn "could they make it flare up?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "bhabbo nu kho so puriso parittaṁ aggiṁ ujjāletun”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:8.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.53-9.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.53 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.53:9.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“In the same way, when the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Evameva kho, bhikkhave, yasmiṁ samaye līnaṁ cittaṁ hoti, kālo tasmiṁ samaye dhammavicayasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo vīriyasambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya, kālo pītisambojjhaṅgassa bhāvanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.53/en/sujato#sn46.53:9.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by love developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, mettācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by love together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu mettāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "mettāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.8" ;
    dho:textEn "If they wish: ‘May I meditate staying equanimous, mindful and aware, shunning both the repulsive and the unrepulsive,’ that’s what they do."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sace ākaṅkhati ‘appaṭikūlañca paṭikūlañca tadubhayaṁ abhinivajjetvā upekkhako vihareyyaṁ sato sampajāno’ti, upekkhako ca tattha viharati sato sampajāno, subhaṁ vā kho pana vimokkhaṁ upasampajja viharati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.9" ;
    dho:textEn "The apex of the heart’s release by love is the beautiful, I say, for a wise mendicant here who has not penetrated to a higher freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Subhaparamāhaṁ, bhikkhave, mettācetovimuttiṁ vadāmi, idhapaññassa bhikkhuno uttarivimuttiṁ appaṭivijjhato."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by compassion developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, karuṇācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by compassion together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu karuṇāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "karuṇāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.6" ;
    dho:textEn "Or else, going totally beyond perceptions of form, with the disappearance of perceptions of impingement, not focusing on perceptions of diversity, aware that ‘space is infinite’, they enter and remain in the dimension of infinite space."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sabbaso vā pana rūpasaññānaṁ samatikkamā paṭighasaññānaṁ atthaṅgamā nānattasaññānaṁ amanasikārā ‘ananto ākāso’ti ākāsānañcāyatanaṁ upasampajja viharati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.7" ;
    dho:textEn "The apex of the heart’s release by compassion is the dimension of infinite space, I say, for a wise mendicant here who has not penetrated to a higher freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ākāsānañcāyatanaparamāhaṁ, bhikkhave, karuṇācetovimuttiṁ vadāmi, idhapaññassa bhikkhuno uttarivimuttiṁ appaṭivijjhato."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by rejoicing developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, muditācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by rejoicing together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu muditāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "muditāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.6" ;
    dho:textEn "Or else, going totally beyond the dimension of infinite space, aware that ‘consciousness is infinite’, they enter and remain in the dimension of infinite consciousness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sabbaso vā pana ākāsānañcāyatanaṁ samatikkamma ‘anantaṁ viññāṇan’ti viññāṇañcāyatanaṁ upasampajja viharati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.7" ;
    dho:textEn "The apex of the heart’s release by rejoicing is the dimension of infinite consciousness, I say, for a wise mendicant here who has not penetrated to a higher freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Viññāṇañcāyatanaparamāhaṁ, bhikkhave, muditācetovimuttiṁ vadāmi, idhapaññassa bhikkhuno uttarivimuttiṁ appaṭivijjhato."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by equanimity developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, upekkhācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.10 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.10" ;
    dho:textEn "The apex of the heart’s release by equanimity is the dimension of nothingness, I say, for a wise mendicant here who has not penetrated to a higher freedom.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ākiñcaññāyatanaparamāhaṁ, bhikkhave, upekkhācetovimuttiṁ vadāmi, idhapaññassa bhikkhuno uttarivimuttiṁ appaṭivijjhato”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.10"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by equanimity together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu upekkhāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.9 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.9" ;
    dho:textEn "Or else, going totally beyond the dimension of infinite consciousness, aware that ‘there is nothing at all’, they enter and remain in the dimension of nothingness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sabbaso vā pana viññāṇañcāyatanaṁ samatikkamma ‘natthi kiñcī’ti ākiñcaññāyatanaṁ upasampajja viharati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-1.10 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:1.10" ;
    dho:textEn "“Prince, there are causes and reasons for not knowing and not seeing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Atthi, rājakumāra, hetu, atthi paccayo aññāṇāya adassanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:1.10"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-1.11 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:1.11" ;
    dho:textEn "Not knowing and not seeing have causes and reasons."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sahetu, sappaccayo aññāṇaṁ adassanaṁ hoti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:1.11"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-1.12 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:1.12" ;
    dho:textEn "There are causes and reasons for knowing and seeing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, rājakumāra, hetu, atthi paccayo ñāṇāya dassanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:1.12"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-1.13 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:1.13" ;
    dho:textEn "Knowing and seeing have causes and reasons.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sahetu, sappaccayo ñāṇaṁ dassanaṁ hotī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:1.13"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "“There’s a time when the heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire, without truly knowing and seeing the escape from sensual desire that has arisen."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Yasmiṁ kho, rājakumāra, samaye kāmarāgapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati kāmarāgaparetena, uppannassa ca kāmarāgassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "This is a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo aññāṇāya adassanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "doubt, without truly knowing and seeing the escape from doubt that has arisen."@en ;
    dho:textPi "vicikicchāpariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati vicikicchāparetena, uppannāya ca vicikicchāya nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-3.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:3.5" ;
    dho:textEn "This is a cause and reason for not knowing and not seeing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo aññāṇāya adassanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:3.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-5.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:5.3" ;
    dho:textEn "“It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Idha, rājakumāra, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:5.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-5.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:5.4" ;
    dho:textEn "They truly know and see with a mind that has developed the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en ;
    dho:textPi "So satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāvitena cittena yathābhūtaṁ jānāti passati—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:5.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-5.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:5.5" ;
    dho:textEn "This is a cause and reason for knowing and seeing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo ñāṇāya dassanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:5.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-6.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:6.2" ;
    dho:textEn "equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:6.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-6.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:6.3" ;
    dho:textEn "They truly know and see with a mind that has developed the awakening factor of equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "So upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāvitena cittena yathābhūtaṁ jānāti passati—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:6.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.56-6.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.56 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.56:6.4" ;
    dho:textEn "This is a cause and reason for knowing and seeing."@en ;
    dho:textPi "ayampi kho, rājakumāra, hetu, ayaṁ paccayo ñāṇāya dassanāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato#sn46.56:6.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahapphalā hoti mahānisaṁsā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of a skeleton together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-1.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:1.6" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the perception of a skeleton, when developed and cultivated, is very fruitful and beneficial.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahapphalā hoti mahānisaṁsā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:1.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“When the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated you can expect one of two results: enlightenment in this very life, or if there’s residue left behind, non-return."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññāya, bhikkhave, bhāvitāya bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.3" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.5" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitāya kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññāya evaṁ bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated it leads to great benefit."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahato atthāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:3.3" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:3.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-3.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:3.5" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahato atthāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:3.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-4.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:4.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated it leads to great sanctuary from the yoke."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahato yogakkhemāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:4.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-4.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:4.3" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:4.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-4.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:4.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:4.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-4.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:4.5" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahato yogakkhemāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:4.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-5.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:5.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated it leads to great inspiration."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahato saṁvegāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:5.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-5.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:5.3" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:5.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-5.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:5.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:5.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-5.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:5.5" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahato saṁvegāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:5.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-6.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:6.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated it leads to dwelling in great ease."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahato phāsuvihārāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:6.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-6.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:6.3" ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:6.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-6.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:6.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:6.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-6.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:6.5" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahato phāsuvihārāya saṁvattatī”ti"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:6.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.58-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.58 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.58:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a worm-infested corpse is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Puḷavakasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.58/en/sujato#sn46.58:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.59-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.59 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.59:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a livid corpse is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Vinīlakasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.59/en/sujato#sn46.59:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“But what things must be developed and cultivated in order to fulfill knowledge and freedom?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Katame pana, bho gotama, dhammā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiṁ paripūrentī”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“The seven awakening factors.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Satta kho, kuṇḍaliya, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiṁ paripūrentī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "“But what things must be developed and cultivated in order to fulfill the seven awakening factors?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Katame pana, bho gotama, dhammā bhāvitā bahulīkatā satta bojjhaṅge paripūrentī”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "“The four kinds of mindfulness meditation.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Cattāro kho, kuṇḍaliya, satipaṭṭhānā bhāvitā bahulīkatā satta bojjhaṅge paripūrentī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "“But what things must be developed and cultivated in order to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Katame pana, bho gotama, dhammā bhāvitā, bahulīkatā cattāro satipaṭṭhāne paripūrentī”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "“The three kinds of good conduct.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Tīṇi kho, kuṇḍaliya, sucaritāni bhāvitāni bahulīkatāni cattāro satipaṭṭhāne paripūrentī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.7" ;
    dho:textEn "“But what things must be developed and cultivated in order to fulfill the three kinds of good conduct?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Katame pana, bho gotama, dhammā bhāvitā bahulīkatā tīṇi sucaritāni paripūrentī”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.8" ;
    dho:textEn "“Sense restraint."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Indriyasaṁvaro kho, kuṇḍaliya, bhāvito bahulīkato tīṇi sucaritāni paripūretīti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And Kuṇḍaliya, how is sense restraint developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the three kinds of good conduct?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvito ca, kuṇḍaliya, indriyasaṁvaro kathaṁ bahulīkato tīṇi sucaritāni paripūretīti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-5.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:5.7" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how sense restraint is developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the three kinds of good conduct."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvito kho, kuṇḍaliya, indriyasaṁvaro evaṁ bahulīkato tīṇi sucaritāni paripūreti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:5.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-6.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:6.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how are the three kinds of good conduct developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitāni ca, kuṇḍaliya, tīṇi sucaritāni kathaṁ bahulīkatāni cattāro satipaṭṭhāne paripūrenti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:6.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-6.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:6.2" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant gives up bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind, and develops good conduct by way of body, speech, and mind."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, kuṇḍaliya, bhikkhu kāyaduccaritaṁ pahāya kāyasucaritaṁ bhāveti, vacīduccaritaṁ pahāya vacīsucaritaṁ bhāveti, manoduccaritaṁ pahāya manosucaritaṁ bhāveti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:6.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-6.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:6.3" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the three kinds of good conduct are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitāni kho, kuṇḍaliya, tīṇi sucaritāni evaṁ bahulīkatāni cattāro satipaṭṭhāne paripūrenti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:6.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-7.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:7.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how are the four kinds of mindfulness meditation developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the seven awakening factors?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, kuṇḍaliya, cattāro satipaṭṭhānā kathaṁ bahulīkatā satta bojjhaṅge paripūrenti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:7.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-7.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:7.2" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of the body—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, kuṇḍaliya, bhikkhu kāye kāyānupassī viharati ātāpī sampajāno satimā, vineyya loke abhijjhādomanassaṁ;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:7.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-7.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:7.3" ;
    dho:textEn "They meditate observing an aspect of feelings …"@en ;
    dho:textPi "vedanāsu …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:7.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-7.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:7.4" ;
    dho:textEn "mind …"@en ;
    dho:textPi "citte …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:7.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-7.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:7.5" ;
    dho:textEn "principles—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world."@en ;
    dho:textPi "dhammesu dhammānupassī viharati ātāpī sampajāno satimā, vineyya loke abhijjhādomanassaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:7.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-7.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:7.6" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the four kinds of mindfulness meditation are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, kuṇḍaliya, cattāro satipaṭṭhānā evaṁ bahulīkatā satta bojjhaṅge paripūrenti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:7.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-8.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:8.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how are the seven awakening factors developed and cultivated so as to fulfill knowledge and freedom?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, kuṇḍaliya, satta bojjhaṅgā kathaṁ bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiṁ paripūrenti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:8.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-8.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:8.2" ;
    dho:textEn "A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, kuṇḍaliya, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:8.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-8.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:8.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:8.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-8.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:8.4" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill knowledge and freedom.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, kuṇḍaliya, satta bojjhaṅgā evaṁ bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiṁ paripūrentī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:8.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.60-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.60 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.60:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a split open corpse is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Vicchiddakasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.60/en/sujato#sn46.60:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.61-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.61 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.61:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of a bloated corpse is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Uddhumātakasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.61/en/sujato#sn46.61:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.62-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.62 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.62:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when love is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Mettā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.62/en/sujato#sn46.62:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.63-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.63 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.63:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when compassion is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Karuṇā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.63/en/sujato#sn46.63:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.64-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.64 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.64:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when rejoicing is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Muditā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.64/en/sujato#sn46.64:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.65-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.65 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.65:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when equanimity is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Upekkhā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.65/en/sujato#sn46.65:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.66-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.66 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.66:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when mindfulness of breathing is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ānāpānassati, bhikkhave, bhāvitā …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.66/en/sujato#sn46.66:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.67-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.67 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.67:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of ugliness is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Asubhasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.67/en/sujato#sn46.67:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.68-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.68 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.68:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of death is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Maraṇasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.68/en/sujato#sn46.68:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.69-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.69 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.69:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of repulsiveness of food is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Āhāre paṭikūlasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.69/en/sujato#sn46.69:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.7-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.7 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.7:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, the rafters of a bungalow all slant, slope, and incline to the peak."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, kūṭāgārassa yā kāci gopānasiyo, sabbā tā kūṭaninnā kūṭapoṇā kūṭapabbhārā;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato#sn46.7:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.7-1.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.7 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.7:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satta bojjhaṅge bhāvento satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaronto nibbānaninno hoti nibbānapoṇo nibbānapabbhāro."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato#sn46.7:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.7-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.7 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.7:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato#sn46.7:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.7-2.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.7 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.7:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato#sn46.7:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.7-2.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.7 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.7:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satta bojjhaṅge bhāvento satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaronto nibbānaninno hoti nibbānapoṇo nibbānapabbhāro”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato#sn46.7:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.70-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.70 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.70:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of dissatisfaction with the whole world is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sabbaloke anabhiratisaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.70/en/sujato#sn46.70:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.71-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.71 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.71:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of impermanence is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aniccasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.71/en/sujato#sn46.71:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.72-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.72 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.72:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of suffering in impermanence is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Anicce dukkhasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.72/en/sujato#sn46.72:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.73-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.73 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.73:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of not-self in suffering is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Dukkhe anattasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.73/en/sujato#sn46.73:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.74-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.74 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.74:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of giving up is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pahānasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.74/en/sujato#sn46.74:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.75-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.75 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.75:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of dispassion is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Virāgasaññā, bhikkhave …pe…”"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.75/en/sujato#sn46.75:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated it’s very fruitful and beneficial."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Nirodhasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahapphalā hoti mahānisaṁsā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-1.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of cessation together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-1.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how, when the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated, it’s very fruitful and beneficial."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, nirodhasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahapphalā hoti mahānisaṁsāti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated you can expect one of two results:"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Nirodhasaññāya, bhikkhave, bhāvitāya bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "enlightenment in this very life, or if there’s residue left behind, non-return."@en ;
    dho:textPi "diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of cessation together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.7" ;
    dho:textEn "When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated in this way you can expect one of two results:"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitāya kho, bhikkhave, nirodhasaññāya evaṁ bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.8" ;
    dho:textEn "enlightenment in this very life, or if there’s residue left behind, non-return.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitāti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“The perception of cessation, when developed and cultivated, leads to great benefit … great sanctuary from the yoke … great inspiration … great ease."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Nirodhasaññā, bhikkhave, bhāvitā bahulīkatā mahato atthāya saṁvattati, mahato yogakkhemāya saṁvattati, mahato saṁvegāya saṁvattati, mahato phāsuvihārāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of cessation together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.5 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.5" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how the perception of cessation, when developed and cultivated, leads to great benefit … great sanctuary from the yoke … great inspiration … great ease.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitā kho, bhikkhave, nirodhasaññā evaṁ bahulīkatā mahato atthāya saṁvattati, mahato yogakkhemāya saṁvattati, mahato saṁvegāya saṁvattati, mahato phāsuvihārāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.8-2.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.8 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.8:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Reverend Upavāṇa, can a mendicant know that by investigating inside themselves, the seven awakening factors have been properly implemented so that they lead to living at ease?”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Jāneyya nu kho, āvuso upavāna, bhikkhu ‘paccattaṁ yonisomanasikārā evaṁ susamāraddhā me satta bojjhaṅgā phāsuvihārāya saṁvattantī’”ti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.8/en/sujato#sn46.8:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.8-2.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.8 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.8:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“They can, Reverend Sāriputta."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Jāneyya kho, āvuso sāriputta, bhikkhu ‘paccattaṁ yonisomanasikārā evaṁ susamāraddhā me satta bojjhaṅgā phāsuvihārāya saṁvattantī’”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.8/en/sujato#sn46.8:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.8-3.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.8 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.8:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "That’s how a mendicant can know that by investigating inside themselves, the seven awakening factors are properly implemented so that they lead to living at ease.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Evaṁ kho, āvuso sāriputta, bhikkhu jāneyya ‘paccattaṁ yonisomanasikārā evaṁ susamāraddhā me satta bojjhaṅgā phāsuvihārāya saṁvattantī’”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.8/en/sujato#sn46.8:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

